@startuml agent-roles
title Recommended flow between the agents (~/.claude/agents)

floating note left
  The main session runs every agent and
  relays its questions to the user;
  agents never call each other.

  **Commits** wait for the user's approval,
  unless the user said "feel free to commit".
  Only the user pushes.

  **rubber-duck**: any time someone is stuck
  (notes: docs/notes/rubber-duck.md).
end note

start

partition "1. Vision" {
  repeat
    :**product-manager**: questions, then options and a pick
    (memory: docs/VISION.draft.md, diagrams: docs/vision/);
    :**user**: answers;
    :**devils-advocate**: challenges the chosen direction;
  repeat while (user agrees to the vision?) is (no) not (yes)
  :**product-manager**: renames the draft to docs/VISION.md,
  commits it once the user approves;
}

partition "2. Architecture" {
  repeat
    :**architect**: questions, then options and a pick
    (memory: docs/ARCHITECTURE.draft.md, diagrams: docs/architecture/);
    :**user**: answers;
    :**devils-advocate**: challenges the design and the plan;
  repeat while (user agrees to the architecture?) is (no) not (yes)
  :**architect**: renames the draft to docs/ARCHITECTURE.md,
  writes a plan file per step: docs/plans/NN-name.md (Status: todo),
  commits them once the user approves;
}

partition "3. Each step (docs/plans/NN-name.md)" {
  repeat
    :**engineer**: creates the step's log, docs/plans/NN-name.log.md;
    note right
      The log is the step's shared memory: every
      agent on the step reads it, and the ones that
      write append an entry. It is never committed.
    end note
    repeat
      :**engineer**: implements the step, or fixes the findings,
      left uncommitted;
      note right
        If the step can't be done as planned,
        the engineer stops and the **architect**
        fixes the plan file first.
      end note
      :**tester**: writes and runs the tests,
      updates docs/TESTING.md;
      :**code-reviewer**: reviews the step's code and tests;
    repeat while (findings or failing tests?) is (yes) not (no)
    :**documenter**: README, developer docs, CHANGELOG.md,
    docs/DESIGN.md (as built, with diagrams in docs/design/);
    :**engineer**: once the user approves, marks the step done
    (plan file Status, tick in ARCHITECTURE.md), makes one local
    commit (code, tests, docs) and deletes the log;
  repeat while (more steps?) is (yes) not (no)
}

partition "4. Before pushing" {
  :**devils-advocate**: challenges the finished work;
  :**user**: pushes;
}

stop
@enduml
